  "reason": "The current best is config_029 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, 0.7250 acc) with config_007 (same but concat fusion, 0.7207) very close. The evidence strongly identifies scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l as the optimal encoder pair, with transformer aggregation and weighted fusion as the best aggregation/fusion choices. Config_010 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + concat) is the one remaining cell in the 2×2 aggregation×fusion grid for this encoder pair, completing the design-space evidence. While it is unlikely to surpass config_029 (avgpool underperformed transformer by ~0.02 in config_048 vs 029, and concat underperformed weighted by ~0.004 in config_007 vs 029), it is the most informative and cheapest remaining experiment (~4–5 GPU hours, comparable to config_048's 4.82 hrs) in the primary design space. Running it now leaves the final experiment free to either exploit a surprise or perform a targeted confirmation, making this the best use of experiment 9 under the 1-experiment-remaining constraint."
